      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test file and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that when ASCII charset is configured, the section sign character `§` (U+00A7) in a string is escaped to the HTML entity `&sect;`. I'll rewrite it with clear variable names and a descriptive comment.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test uses clear variable names (`asciiOutputSettings`, `inputWithSectionSign`, `escaped`), removes the unnecessary intermediate variable (`document_OutputSettings1` was just the same object returned by `charset()`), uses the literal `§` character instead of the opaque unicode escape `\\u00A7`, and adds descriptive comments explaining why ASCII charset forces HTML entity escaping and what the expected output means."
